&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;I understand that I am applying for employment with Ginkgo Bioworks and am being asked to provide information in connection with my application. I further understand that Ginkgo gathers this information through a third-party service provider and that Ginkgo may also use other service providers to assist in the application process.&amp;nbsp; Ginkgo may share my information with such third-party service providers in connection with my application and for the start of employment.&amp;nbsp; Ginkgo will treat my information in accordance with Ginkgo&#39;s &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ginkgobioworks.com/concentric-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp; By submitting this job application, I am acknowledging that I have reviewed and agree to Ginkgo&#39;s &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ginkgobioworks.com/concentric-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; as well as the privacy policies of the third-party service providers used by Ginkgo&#39;s associated with the application process.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to make biology easier to engineer. Ginkgo is constructing, editing, and redesigning the living world in order to answer the globe’s growing challenges in health, energy, food, materials, and more. Our bioengineers make use of an in-house automated foundry for designing and building new organisms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;As a Product Manager on the Reagents team, you will own one or more product lines end-to-end—from customer discovery and roadmap definition through launch, growth, and ongoing customer success. We are a small, high-ownership team, so this role spans the full commercial surface of the business: product management, marketing, e-commerce and commercial operations, and customer success. You will partner closely with our science, foundry operations, supply chain, and engineering teams to bring new reagent products to market, scale the ones already in customers’ hands, and continuously improve the experience scientists have with Ginkgo Reagents.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;This is a hands-on role for someone who wants to combine strategic product thinking with operational execution. You will be expected to set the direction for your product area, then roll up your sleeves to make it happen—writing PRDs, talking to customers, pricing kits, fixing a stuck order, and shipping a launch campaign all in the same week.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Product Discovery &amp;amp; Roadmap&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Customer Discovery: Run customer interviews, voice-of-customer programs, and market research with scientists at academic labs, pharma and biotech R&amp;amp;D teams, and AI-driven discovery companies to deeply understand workflows, unmet needs, and willingness to pay.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roadmap Ownership: Define and own the product roadmap for your area (e.g., cell-free protein synthesis, PichiaWorks, proteins and enzymes); prioritize ruthlessly across new products, formats, and improvements based on customer value, commercial impact, and feasibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Requirements &amp;amp; Specs: Write clear product requirements (PRDs, user stories, success criteria) and partner with science and operations teams to translate them into manufacturable, automation-friendly products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Market &amp;amp; Competitive Intelligence: Build and maintain a current view of the competitive landscape, pricing, and emerging customer segments; use it to inform roadmap and positioning decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Launch &amp;amp; Go-to-Market&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Launch Ownership: Drive product launches end-to-end—launch plan, readiness checklist, cross-functional coordination, internal enablement, and post-launch tracking.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Positioning &amp;amp; Messaging: Develop positioning, value propositions, and messaging tailored to target customer segments, and translate them into customer-facing assets in partnership with marketing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pricing &amp;amp; Packaging: Set and iterate on pricing, packaging, and bundling decisions based on customer research, competitive benchmarks, and unit economics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Commercial Operations &amp;amp; E-commerce&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Storefront Ownership: Own the e-commerce experience on the Reagents storefront, including product pages, SKU setup, content quality, and conversion optimization (Shopify/ERP).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Order &amp;amp; Fulfillment Operations: Partner with Foundry operations, supply chain, and shipping to ensure orders flow accurately, cold-chain requirements are met, and shipments dispatch on time; troubleshoot bottlenecks as they arise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Inventory &amp;amp; Demand Planning: Monitor stock levels of high-demand kits and reagents, forecast demand, and partner with operations to prevent out-of-stock scenarios and right-size inventory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Metrics &amp;amp; Analytics: Define and track the KPIs for your area, such as revenue, conversion, fulfillment SLAs, NPS, repeat rate, and use them to inform roadmap and operational decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Marketing &amp;amp; Customer Success&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Content &amp;amp; Demand Generation: Own product content end-to-end, including product pages, technical specs, application notes, blog posts, and email and social campaigns—optimized for SEO (search engine optimization) and AEO (answer engine optimization) across Google, ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, and Google AI Overviews.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead Generation &amp;amp; Pipeline: Identify high-potential customer segments and accounts, run targeted outreach, and partner with the commercial team to convert interest into orders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Customer Success: Be a strong voice for the customer, own the inbound support experience, coordinate with internal scientists on technical questions, and run a structured post-purchase feedback loop to drive product and experience improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Conferences &amp;amp; Field Engagement: Represent Ginkgo Reagents at industry conferences and customer meetings, generate target lists for new partnership opportunities, and build relationships with key accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MS or PhD in a life sciences field (e.g., biology, biochemistry, molecular or cell biology, bioengineering, synthetic biology) OR an MBA, product, or marketing degree paired with demonstrated experience in life sciences tools or reagents&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;3–5 years of product management, product marketing, or commercial experience, ideally in life sciences tools, reagents, diagnostics, or scientific instrumentation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Track record of owning a product or product line end-to-end, from discovery and roadmap through launch and post-launch growth&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong customer discovery and research instincts; comfortable talking to PhD-level scientists about their workflows and translating that into product decisions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong quantitative and analytical skills; comfortable building business cases, sizing markets, and analyzing product and operational metrics&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication, with the ability to write professionally and clearly to a scientific (including PhD-level) audience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;High-ownership, entrepreneurial mindset, comfortable operating in a small team, wearing multiple hats, and moving fluidly between strategy and execution&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Eligible to work in the United States; this role is based in Boston, Massachusetts&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prior experience launching reagent or kit products, ideally in protein expression, enzymes, cell-free systems, or AI-driven protein screening workflows&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hands-on experience with e-commerce platforms (e.g., Shopify), ERPs, and CRM tools (e.g., HubSpot, Salesforce)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working knowledge of SEO and AEO best practices—including keyword research, on-page SEO, structured data/schema, and content optimization for AI answer engines—and hands-on experience with tools such as Google Search Console, Google Analytics, Ahrefs, SEMrush, or Clearscope&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with cold-chain logistics, demand planning, or other operational aspects of a physical-product business&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bench experience in molecular or cell biology, biochemistry, or synthetic biology&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Understanding of synthetic biology, drug discovery and development, or the broader life sciences tools market&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong presentation (powerpoint or gslides) and spreadsheet skills (excel or gsheets)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Total compensation for this role is market driven, and includes both salary and company stock awards. Base pay is ultimately determined based on a candidate’s skills, expertise, and experience. We also offer a comprehensive benefits package including medical, dental &amp;amp; vision coverage, health spending accounts, voluntary benefits, leave of absence policies, Employee Assistance Program, 401(k) program with employer contribution, 8 paid holidays in addition to a full-week winter shutdown and unlimited Paid Time Off policy.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ginkgo has implemented a return to office policy effective October 1, 2025. This roll requires will require the employee to be onsite 5 days per week.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;It is the policy of Ginkgo Bioworks to provide equal employment opportunities to all employees, employment applicants, and EOE disability/vet.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
